## PART 1: THE COMPLETE TRANSFORMER PIPELINE

Here is the entire flow from your input to the model's output:

```
INPUT TEXT: "The cat sat on the"
         ↓
    ┌─────────────┐
    │ TOKENIZER   │
    └─────────────┘
         ↓
TOKENS: ["The", " cat", " sat", " on", " the"]
         ↓
    ┌─────────────┐
    │ EMBEDDINGS  │
    └─────────────┘
         ↓
VECTORS: [0.23, -0.45, 0.67, 0.12, -0.89]  (numbers for each token)
         ↓
    ┌─────────────┐
    │ATTENTION    │
    └─────────────┘
         ↓
WEIGHTED RELATIONSHIPS: "cat" ←→ "sat" (strong), "the" → "cat" (medium)
         ↓
    ┌─────────────┐
    │FEED FORWARD │
    │ NETWORK     │
    └─────────────┘
         ↓
PROCESSED INFORMATION: patterns applied (grammar, facts, logic)
         ↓
    ┌─────────────┐
    │NEXT TOKEN   │
    │PREDICTION   │
    └─────────────┘
         ↓
PROBABILITIES: "mat" (45%), "floor" (30%), "chair" (15%), others (10%)
         ↓
    ┌─────────────┐
    │  OUTPUT     │
    └─────────────┘
         ↓
GENERATED TEXT: "The cat sat on the mat"
```

**Key insight:** After outputting one token, the model adds it to the input and repeats the entire pipeline until it decides to stop.

